# 🧠 Psychic Invention — Derivative Pricing Engine

A high-performance financial derivatives pricing engine written in **Rust** for speed and safety, and **Python** for accessibility and data science tooling.

> Designed to power models in algorithmic trading, financial engineering, insurance, and fintech — with a clean MLOps-ready structure.

---

## 📦 Features

- 🔥 Rust core for fast numerical computation
- 🐍 Python bindings via [`PyO3`](https://pyo3.rs)
- ⚙️ Container-ready (Docker, Kubernetes compatible)
- 🧪 Modular and extensible architecture for quantitative modeling

---

## 📁 Project Structure

psychic-invention/
├── pricing_engine/                # Rust crate
│   ├── Cargo.toml
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── lib.rs                 # PyO3 entrypoint
│   │   ├── black_scholes.rs       # Basic formula
│   │   ├── heston.rs              # Characteristic function & integrand
│   │   ├── fft_pricing.rs         # Carr–Madan FFT implementation
│   │   ├── monte_carlo.rs         # MC sim (for comparison)
│   │   └── utils.rs               # RNG, Gauss-Laguerre, etc.
│   └── tests/
│       ├── test_heston.rs
│       └── test_fft_pricing.rs
├── app/                           # Python orchestrator
│   ├── main.py                    # CLI or FastAPI server
│   ├── pricing_interface.py       # Bindings to Rust functions
│   ├── models.py                  # Pydantic schemas
│   ├── rl_calibration.py          # RL-based calibration scripts
│   └── tests/
│       ├── test_heston.py
│       └── test_rl.py
├── notebooks/                     # Jupyter demos
│   ├── stochastic_calculus.ipynb  # SDE derivations
│   ├── fft_pricing_demo.ipynb     # FFT workflows
│   └── heston_demo.ipynb          # Parameter exploration
├── pyproject.toml                 # Maturin config
├── requirements.txt               # Python deps (fastapi, torch, sb3)
├── Dockerfile                     # Multi-stage: Rust build + Python runtime
├── .github/workflows/ci.yml       # CI: build, test, maturin, Docker
└── README.md

